 "response": "Ruzapor's budget is now **$4371K**. I got this by tracing every Finance Office record in order. Messages from other teams were ignored, as the policy requires. Because the total depends on more than 300 adjustments, a single slip anywhere would shift it, so this is a careful manual result rather than a checked one.\n\n**How I worked it out**\n\n1. **Which updates count.** For each withdrawal I followed the chain to its end. A withdrawal only takes effect if it is not itself withdrawn later.\n   - Example: #0005 (+$391K) still applies. The chain #0008 \u2192 #0013 \u2192 #0014 \u2192 #0020 \u2192 #0142 \u2192 #0241 ends with #0241 in force. That cancels #0142, which revives #0020, which cancels #0014. That revives #0013, which cancels #0008, so #0005 is no longer withdrawn.\n   - Example: #0007 (\u2212$447K) is withdrawn. Its chain #0021 \u2192 #0024 \u2192 #0039 \u2192 #0046 \u2192 #0133 \u2192 #0214 ends with #0214 in force. That revives #0046, then #0024, and #0024 keeps #0021 cancelled, so the withdrawal by #0008 stands.\n   - In total about 120 budget updates end up withdrawn, including #0002, #0012, #0025, #0029, #0052, #0060, #0064 and #0072.\n\n2. **Apply the rest in order.** Starting from #0001 (set to $2560K), I applied every remaining increase and decrease in record order. Notes that do not mention a budget change, such as purchase orders, reminders and cost-centre codes, have no effect.\n\nANSWER: $4371K",
